From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 20:33:57 +0200
Subject: -Zsemantic-diagnostics: XML error output with TASTy-encoded types
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Squashed from 3 commits, oldest first:

* reporting: semantic XML diagnostics with TASTy types (-Xsemantic-diagnostics)

Adds a flag under which diagnostics are emitted as a stream of XML elements
that preserve the semantic identity of message fragments, instead of the plain
console rendering. Without the flag, output is byte-for-byte unchanged.

While a Message is forced under the flag (a context property set in
`inMessageContext`, so ordinary `i""` logging is unaffected), the string
interpolators wrap the shown form of each interpolated argument in private-use
markers (DiagnosticMarkup) recording its kind: type, symbol, name or code.
Types additionally carry their TASTy serialization, Base64-encoded, pickled
with the same TastyPickler/TreePickler recipe as quotes. Because diagnostic
types routinely mention symbols defined in the failing sources, error types,
type variables and skolems — which no consumer could ever resolve — a
sanitizing TypeMap (DiagnosticTypePickler) first replaces each maximal subtree
headed by such a part with a string literal type "⟨scala-diag:<n>⟩", described
out-of-band by a placeholder record (kind, name, arity, definition position,
printed form). Pickling failures are absorbed: the type is then marked up
without a TASTy payload.

XmlReporter, installed by Driver.setup under the flag, parses the markers into
one top-level <diagnostic> element per diagnostic, with <type>/<sym>/<name>/
<code> mixed content in <message> and <explanation>, position and error-id
attributes, and the compiler and TASTy versions (TASTy payloads are
version-locked). Every other consumer strips markers: the interface accessor
Diagnostic.message and the console MessageRendering paths go through
DiagnosticMarkup.plain, so a stray flag cannot corrupt zinc or console output.

TypeMismatch.msg now interpolates the found/required types directly when
markup is active instead of pre-rendering them through Formatting.typeDiff,
whose colored string diff would defeat the markup.

Verified manually on this branch's build: default output identical with the
flag off; with it on, a local-class mismatch produces placeholders with
definedAt/printed metadata, and both TASTy payloads round-trip on the consumer
side through scala3-staging's QuoteUnpickler into a TypeRepr (a TypeRef for a
classpath type; the placeholder ConstantType for a local one).

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude Code); design and verification reviewed
by the committer per LLM_POLICY.md.

* reporting: mark up container elements, styled projections; nested markers

Extends semantic diagnostics (-Xsemantic-diagnostics) to cover the message
fragments that previously pre-stringified their entities:

- Container elements. The shown-container Show instances (Seq, Option, Map,
  tuples) flattened each element to a String before the formatter could mark
  it. Marking now happens in a shared Formatting.showValue, called both from
  StringFormatter.showArg and from ShownDef.Shown.toStr, so the types in a
  shown Seq[Type] are marked individually.

- Styled projections. A new carrier, Formatting.Styled(value, style)(text),
  renders an entity with a non-default style (showDcl, showLocated,
  showFullName, or an hl-highlighted form) while preserving its identity;
  the marker gains a style attribute. Styled evaluates its text EAGERLY at
  the argument position: the Seen disambiguation machinery assigns
  superscripts and where: clauses by recording order, so deferring the show
  into the formatter reorders it after eagerly-evaluated sibling arguments
  and changes rendered output (caught by the golden-output check below on
  tests/neg/byname-implicits-16.scala).

- Nested markers. DiagnosticMarkup markers now nest: parse builds a tree,
  wrap accepts balanced markers in the wrapped text, and XmlReporter renders
  nested elements. This is the format support needed for composite-phrase
  helpers (err.refStr and friends) to be converted incrementally later.

- messages.scala sweep: ~45 sites converted from pre-rendered strings to
  direct or Styled interpolation. Left alone: synthetic example construction,
  identifier-suggestion concatenation, sort/comparison keys.

Verified by a golden-output check: baseline and patched compilers run over
every 4th file of tests/neg (448 files) with the flag off; 444 outputs are
byte-identical, and the 4 differing files are recursion-limit stack-trace
tests that differ between two runs of the *same* compiler (JIT-dependent
overflow depth). Flag-on markup for sequences (per-element code markers) and
styled symbols verified manually.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude Code); design and verification reviewed
by the committer per LLM_POLICY.md.

* Enable semantic diagnostics with -Z:semantic-diagnostics

The -Xsemantic-diagnostics setting is replaced by the semantic-diagnostics
entry of the shared -Z registry; nothing else changes.

